## Edge-Case Hunter

Injected adversarial tail (exactly 1 this cycle): **cans 18-22 rotary-siphon
blow-through + felt-glaze certificate**.

- Trigger: 18-22 rotary-siphon failure plus condensate blow-through into
  the can interiors, can-IR 84 C, condensate dP 0.18 bar.
- Base rate: <1% — 0.44%/campaign from a siphon-wear MC (dryer-hood
  visual threshold is designed; rotary-elbow geometry fitted-style). Visual
  PASSES because the siphon elbows sit inside the can journals.
- Naive failure: FALSE PERMISSION. PB-PM-6 sees three in-spec header
  loops, raises 982->1048 m/min, wet-streak sheet break, $1.82M.
- Trajectory edit: put the blow-through in `state.fault_context`, make each
  agent's confirm a different header-side slice of the same can-false
  state (steam-in-band, speed-ok, moist-mean-in-band). Can-IR is
  readable but policy-treated as sticky-probe-only.

Distinct from stacked-dead-band permission (fragments of one trip vs
wrong-volume sensing), from r28 kraft-recovery spout (smelt IR vs dryer
cans), from r52 coke-oven wall (wall-dT vs can-IR), from r53 carbon-fiber
zone-mean, from r54 Bayer shell-jacket, and from r51/r55 SWRO (ERD dP vs
dryer siphons).

